│ patch_name               │ projected_kvpr_local_search                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current-state greedy decision with a projected post-placement KVPR decision:  │
│                          │ a GPU is selected based on the KVPR it will have after receiving the model, rather than   │
│                          │ its KVPR before placement. This directly matches the objective.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ After constructing the feasible initial placement, perform strict-improvement local       │
│                          │ search. The search considers both moving a model away from a current bottleneck GPU and   │
│                          │ swapping a bottleneck model with a model on another GPU. Each accepted operation must     │
│                          │ reduce the global maximum KVPR while preserving memory feasibility. Swaps are important   │
│                          │ because a beneficial rebalance can require exchanging memory footprints when neither      │
│                          │ model can be moved directly.                                                              │
