│ patch_description        │ Replace the current-state greedy rule with projected KVPR minimization: every candidate   │
│                          │ GPU is evaluated using the KVPR it will have after receiving the model, while also        │
│                          │ accounting for the maximum KVPR on all other GPUs. This directly optimizes the stated     │
│                          │ minimax objective instead of selecting the least-loaded GPU before placement.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Use several deterministic ordering strategies because memory fragmentation makes a single │
│                          │ model order unreliable. The best feasible resulting placement is retained. A final        │
│                          │ relocation pass moves models when doing so strictly reduces the global maximum KVPR,      │
│                          │ improving allocations missed by the initial greedy construction while preserving all      │
│                          │ memory constraints.                                                                       │
