│ patch_name               │ lex_exchange_balancer                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This version combines multi-start pressure-aware construction with a lexicographic        │
│                          │ local-search objective. Instead of accepting only moves that immediately reduce the       │
│                          │ single worst KVPR, it minimizes the sorted vector of GPU pressures: first the worst GPU,  │
│                          │ then the second worst, and so on. This helps escape placements where the maximum KVPR     │
│                          │ cannot improve until pressure is redistributed among several GPUs.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The construction phase uses several complementary orderings, including pressure-heavy,    │
│                          │ memory-heavy, density-heavy, and mixed priority orders. The refinement phase supports     │
│                          │ moves, one-for-one swaps, bounded one-for-two exchanges, and the recommended reverse      │
│                          │ bounded two-for-one exchanges. All exchanges perform exact memory-capacity checks before  │
│                          │ acceptance.                                                                               │
