│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses five static ordering seeds, two tie modes, and local            │
│                          │ move/swap/one-for-two exchange search with a `3 * model_count` iteration limit. This      │
│                          │ revision keeps the successful lexicographic local-search strategy while expanding         │
│                          │ initialization to eight pressure-aware and capacity-aware orderings. New seeds prioritize │
│                          │ models by `weight / (80 - size)`, pressure with size secondary ordering,                  │
│                          │ pressure-density, and large-model pressure risk. The local-search limit is increased to   │
│                          │ `4 * model_count` so neutral lexicographic improvements have more opportunity to unlock a │
│                          │ lower maximum KVPR. Model weights and sizes are precomputed, reducing repeated attribute  │
│                          │ and division work during search.                                                          │
