│ patch_description        │ Add a targeted refinement pass when direct moves, swaps, and ejection chains cannot       │
│                          │ improve the placement. The remaining local optimum can be caused by a large high-demand   │
│                          │ model on a bottleneck GPU that cannot move alone, while replacing it with two smaller     │
│                          │ models from another GPU would balance both memory headroom and demand.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new pass ranks models on bottleneck GPUs by a combined demand-and-size score,         │
│                          │ considers only the top few, and evaluates feasible one-for-two exchanges against          │
│                          │ high-impact counterpart models. This keeps compound-search runtime bounded while          │
│                          │ addressing capacity barriers that pairwise swaps cannot resolve. Candidate evaluation     │
│                          │ still uses the existing lexicographic KVPR objective and feasibility checker, so every    │
│                          │ accepted refinement strictly improves the placement.                                      │
