│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ three_gpu_ejection_chain                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Add a targeted three-GPU ejection-chain neighborhood after direct moves, swaps, and       │
│                          │ two-for-one exchanges fail. A bottleneck model may be unable to move to a lower-pressure  │
│                          │ GPU solely because that GPU lacks sufficient free memory. This edit tries ejecting one of │
│                          │ the smallest models from that target to a feasible third GPU, then atomically moves the   │
│                          │ bottleneck model into the capacity released on the target.                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The candidate is evaluated using the existing lexicographic KVPR vector, so it is         │
│                          │ accepted only when it strictly improves the current placement. Restricting sources to     │
│                          │ bottleneck GPUs, targets to low-pressure GPUs, victims to the smallest few models, and    │
│                          │ third GPUs to low-pressure candidates keeps the additional search inexpensive.            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
