│ patch_name               │ pressure_repair                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ This version combines objective-aware greedy construction with a deterministic “pressure  │
│                          │ repair” neighborhood search. Inspired by the prior multi-start balancing methods, it      │
│                          │ keeps a small portfolio of high-load, large-model, density, risk, and bucketed            │
│                          │ construction orders. The novel component is a destroy-and-repair step: it temporarily     │
│                          │ removes one or two models from a current bottleneck GPU and greedily reinserts them into  │
│                          │ the whole placement using the full sorted KVPR vector as its objective. This allows       │
│                          │ coordinated relocations that ordinary single moves and swaps cannot reach because of      │
│                          │ memory fragmentation. Every repair is accepted only when it lexicographically improves    │
│                          │ the pressure vector, so the maximum KVPR never worsens.                                   │
