│ patch_description        │ Add a narrowly scoped three-GPU eviction chain after the existing move and swap           │
│                          │ neighborhoods are exhausted. A model on a bottleneck GPU may be unable to fit on a        │
│                          │ lower-pressure GPU because of insufficient free memory. The new step tests evicting one   │
│                          │ model from that target GPU to a feasible third GPU, then placing the bottleneck model     │
│                          │ into the freed space. The entire chain is evaluated atomically against the maximum KVPR   │
│                          │ and is accepted only for a strict improvement. This preserves the inexpensive existing    │
│                          │ local search as the primary strategy while resolving common memory-fragmentation local    │
│                          │ minima.                                                                                   │
